faq.content:
When picking up a postal item, present one of the following documents:

		identity card;
		passport;
		residence permit;
		travel document issued to persons granted refugee status or humanitarian protection;
		driving license.

Parcels, EMS items and cash-on-delivery items may be released to persons other than the addressee only on the basis of a power of attorney drawn up in the established manner.

Registered letter mail items (letters and small packages up to 2 kg), except items marked "Personal delivery", "Summons" or "Notice", may be released without a power of attorney to first and second degree family members who have reached the age of majority, upon presentation of one of the identity documents and a document confirming the family relationship (mother, father, son, daughter, husband, wife, brother, sister, grandfather, grandmother).
